      {
        "name": "methodCopy",
        "data": "1. MEET DETAILS & RULES\nDEMO PRESET\nTHIS IS A DEMO MEET\n\nHidden from the public shows list, DEMO shown on the scoreboard, registration closed. Built from a preset? Flip this before you publish the real thing.\n\nMARK AS REAL MEET\nMEET NAME\nMEET DATE\nURL SLUG (CLOUD SYNC)\nADMIN PIN (4–6 DIGITS)\nCOLLAR WEIGHT / PAIR (LBS)\nRUN ORDER METHODOLOGY (EVENTS 2+)\n\nEvent 1 always runs by lot number. This decides the order for every event after it.\n\nReverse Overall Pts\nReverse Prev Event\nRoster Order\n\nReverse Overall Pts: Lowest overall points lifts first and the current leader goes last. Athletes level on points go by lot number. Most promoters pick this so the podium race builds to the final attempt.\n\nReverse Prev Event: Only the last event counts. Whoever placed last in it goes first and its winner goes last, whatever the overall standings. Athletes tied in that event go lower overall points first, then by lot number.\n\nRoster Order: Athletes go in lot order for every event, never reshuffled. Pick this when the order was published ahead of time.\n\nOVERALL PODIUM TIEBREAKER\n\nUsed only when two athletes finish on the same total points.\n\nMost Event Wins\nFinal Event Score\n\nMost Event Wins: The athlete with more event wins places higher. If that is level too, more points in the final event wins. Still level after both: the athletes share the place.\n\nFinal Event Score: The athlete with more points in the final event places higher. If that is level too, more event wins. Still level after both: the athletes share the place.\n\nAVAILABLE GYM PLATES (TAP TO ENABLE/DISABLE)\n100 lb\n55 lb\n45 lb\n35 lb\n25 lb\n15 lb\n10 lb\n5 lb\n2.5 lb"
      },
